        "original_id": "cde7b43f-beea-560d-9c48-48b8567cf6d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Albert Speer, David Edgar, Gitta Sereny, Mary Bell, Franz Stangl\n- Works: Albert Speer, Albert Speer: His Battle with Truth\n- Roles: playwright, biographer, historian, investigative journalist, architect, commandant\n- Topics: Nazi era, controversial figures, Treblinka extermination camp\n\nFacts:\n- In 1968, Mary Bell was convicted of killing two children when she herself was a child.\n- Gitta Sereny was an Austrian-British biographer, historian, and investigative journalist known for interviews and profiles of controversial figures, including Mary Bell and Franz Stangl.\n- Franz Stangl was the commandant of the Treblinka extermination camp.\n- In 2000, David Edgar's play Albert Speer portrayed the life of Nazi-era architect Albert Speer.\n- The 2000 play Albert Speer by David Edgar was based on Gitta Sereny's book Albert Speer: His Battle with Truth.\n- Gitta Sereny was born on 13 March 1921 and died on 14 June 2012.",
